00:28:48.550 --> 00:28:51.215
I think what we're seeing is
people will usually understand

00:28:51.215 --> 00:28:53.700
ML in one of three ways--
either I hear about this,

00:28:53.700 --> 00:28:56.200
I know I should so it, I have
no idea where to get started--

00:29:00.515 --> 00:29:02.890
I guess the first one is, why
should I be involved in ML?

00:29:02.890 --> 00:29:04.650
The second is, I know I
need to be involved with ML,

00:29:04.650 --> 00:29:06.040
I just don't know
how to get started,

00:29:06.040 --> 00:29:08.165
and three is, I know I need
to be involved with it,

00:29:08.165 --> 00:29:10.585
I know how to get started, now
let's go use Kaggle for it.

00:29:10.585 --> 00:29:12.700
And so I interact with
people on all three

00:29:12.700 --> 00:29:14.470
of those different sides.

00:29:14.470 --> 00:29:16.156
I think, for those
of us who are, maybe,

00:29:16.156 --> 00:29:17.530
in that developer
community, it's

00:29:17.530 --> 00:29:19.240
easy to think, what do you mean?

00:29:19.240 --> 00:29:21.325
People don't get this?

00:29:21.325 --> 00:29:23.950
You have no idea how many times
I have to explain to my parents

00:29:23.950 --> 00:29:26.158
what Kaggle is and they
still don't know what it is--

00:29:26.158 --> 00:29:27.920
or machine learning,
at the least.

00:29:27.920 --> 00:29:31.309
It is growing so
rapidly that we have

00:29:31.309 --> 00:29:33.100
no idea where the
saturation point, really,

00:29:33.100 --> 00:29:34.532
is even going to begin.

